  "body": "## What\n\nAdds a set of **optional** modules to `SKILL.md`, all taken from a real production run: a Spanish zombie-survival short (\"TORRE 12\", 1080x1920, word-synced selection-box captions, SFX-only mix, ElevenLabs narration).\n\n**Nothing in this PR changes the bridge channel's rules** (no captions, English only, music +3 dB mix, 2K export). The new sections are framed as add-on modules for channels that run captions, non-English narration, or no music.\n\n## Why\n\nThe existing skill is proven for one channel style, but running a different channel surfaced a set of concrete, reproducible problems that the current pipeline doesn't cover:\n\n- **ElevenLabs alignment quirk:** the API stores `\"...\"` ellipses as commas, so punctuation-only sentence detection silently fails. A pause-gap rule (>0.3 s between consecutive words) fixes it, verified against real word timings.\n- **Hand-timed scenes drift:** deriving every scene window from the word timings (`start = words[0].ini - 0.25`, monotonic windows) means scenes re-derive automatically when timings change.\n- **Word-synced captions:** a full recipe (grey→white lerp, keyword recolour, selection box on the last-spoken word only), including the hex channel-shift lerp trap that literally turned the word \"zombi\" blue.\n- **Close-up \"half a face\":** facial features drawn past the head circle's edge read as the face sliding off the head. Caught on a rendered frame; fix rule + added to the Readability traps list.\n- **SFX-only mix:** `adelay:all=1` + `amix normalize=0` (normalization squashes the voice under many inputs), mux with `apad`, and a `volumedetect` verification step (SFX window mean −9.5 dB vs −18 dB quiet window).\n- **Thumbnail:** captions are baked into every spoken frame, so the thumbnail needs a code-constant flag (`SIN_SUBS`) — `process.env` does not reach Remotion render workers from a shell one-liner.\n- **Windows/PowerShell gotchas:** the pipeline's Unix patterns (`export TEMP=...`, `cp -f`) need translation on Windows, plus the console backtick-mangling issue that breaks inline JSON edits.\n\n## Changes\n\n- New section `## Optional: caption-channel modules` after Pipeline step 11 (voice, scene timing, captions, close-up trap, SFX mix, thumbnail, frame-review loop)\n- Pipeline steps 3 and 10 cross-reference the new modules\n- 3 Windows/PowerShell entries in `## Gotchas`\n- 1 entry in `## Readability traps` (close-up trap, cross-referenced)\n\n+73 lines, −0 deletions. Docs only — no template or engine code touched, no reference material included.\n",
